#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:5
#: 27d84976c608466794aafc659313c42a
msgid "MAVLink Routing in ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:7
#: dd2e4e57cacc4892bddc0dae5abbd24d
msgid "ArduPilot (which runs on the flight controller) can route MAVLink messages received on one telemetry port to all other telemetry ports.  This is important in cases where there are multiple MAVLink enabled components on the vehicle (i.e. a flight controller and a companion computer) but only a single telemetry connection between the vehicle and the ground station.  This page describes how ArduPilot decides which messages should be routed and to which telemetry ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:13
#: 99ac4ef924604f359e39c334d475b380
msgid "As described on the :ref:`MAVLink Basics <mavlink-basics>` page a MAVLink network is made up of *systems* (vehicles, GCS, antenna trackers, etc) which are themselves made up of *components* (flight controller, camera system, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:15
#: 652781302b06406daa54f2c73218a7d5
msgid "Each message contains a ``System ID`` and ``Component ID`` field to specify where the message came from.  In addition *some messages* (including `SET_POSITION_TARGET_GLOBAL_INT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_POSITION_TARGET_GLOBAL_INT>`__) include ``target_system`` and ``target_component`` fields to allow specifying which system/component should execute the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:17
#: 84eb705dfdb447c198f842537e12e167
msgid "A value of 0 for the ``target_system`` or ``target_component`` is considered a broadcast ID, and will be sent to all systems in the network/components on the target system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:21
#: 259baa05b7a44f609c1d79587cb9e64d
msgid "The routing on ArduPilot systems works in the following way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:23
#: 0e94456255c0476997eaf8792d07632f
msgid "All received MAVLink messages are checked by the `MAVLink_routing <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/GCS_MAVLink/MAVLink_routing.h>`__ class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:24
#: 0695a33f68f84972b7712fc68b73a447
msgid "The class extracts the source system id (aka *sysid*) and component id (aka *compid*) and builds up a routing array which maps the channel (i.e. USB port, Telem1, Telem2) to the *<sysid,compid>* pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:25
#: cdc0227f0e124ab08db8417ee9d69d4d
msgid "The class also extracts the target system id (``target_system``) and component id (``target_component``) and if these don’t match the vehicle’s *<sysid,compid>* the messages are forwarded to the appropriate channel using the array above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:26
#: f1e0df87c9824c5191c8872da2d3f8a1
msgid "Messages that don’t have a target *<sysid,compid>* are processed by the vehicle and then forwarded to each known system/component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mavlink-routing-in-ardupilot.rst:29
#: 6e098c4215e14196971a1707abec5130
msgid "Detailed theory of MAVLink routing"
msgstr ""

